.TH HOMECTL 1
.SH NAME
homectl \- list and inspect accounts through homed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homectl
.RI [ options ]
.RB [ list ]
.br
.B homectl
.RI [ options ]
.B inspect
.I USER
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B homectl
queries the
.B org.freedesktop.home1
service on the system D-Bus.
It can be run as an ordinary user.
Account creation and changes use Slackware's existing account tools.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List accounts returned by the service.
The default output shows the user name, UID, GID, state, home directory, and
shell. With
.BR --json ,
the output is an array of account summaries.
This is the default command.
.TP
.BI inspect " USER"
Show the account record for a user name or numeric UID.
With
.BR --json ,
print the user record as a JSON object.
Use an empty string to select the calling user's account.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print JSON to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the package version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success, one indicates a lookup or runtime error, and two
indicates incorrect usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR homed (8),
.BR userdbctl (1)
